Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Sun Dogs Chew the Coin Slot
- Story & Context: When sixteen-year-old Lyra Vance stripped the corroded harness from an abandoned Ridge Racer unit on the third tier of the Galleria St. Jude, she accidentally shorted the machine's audio board against her Bb clarinet’s copper-bound ligature. The resulting electrical burst blew the mall's dead emergency circuit, filling the cavernous rotunda with the sour smell of fried transformer oil while the gutted cabinet began spitting a continuous, skull-cracking 152 BPM industrial kick-drum loop through the atrium's paging horns. Over the concussive metal-stomp, Lyra blew an overblown multiphonic shriek into the coin slot and screamed into her contact mic: "Breathe down the solder until the glass goes white." By midnight, fifty runaway kids were hauling deep-cycle car batteries across the cracked ceramic tile to dance under the freezing, sun-dog halo formed by winter dawn shining through fractured glass.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: Cinematic macro photography of a vintage arcade coin mechanism choked with melted solder, crystalline frost, and woodwind reeds, glowing with a harsh amber phosphor light while optical sun dog halos reflect off cracked plexiglass.

Track 2: Why Does the Fata Morgana Smell of Ozone?
- Story & Context: Huddled in the drained terrazzo fountain basin behind a derelict Spencer's Gifts, Kaelen Vex wept into his microphone as he recounted stealing his school's contrabass clarinet from a burning band room during the blizzard of 2021. His frostbitten hands rewired an array of six CRT chassis so that every breath through his wooden mouthpiece caused the monitor rasters to ripple and pulse in hypnotic, 64-bar progressive house sweeps. "My throat is an airlock that won't seal shut," he whispered over the sound of sixty teenagers hyperventilating in unison beneath thermal foil capes. The hypnotic, minimal repetition of his woodwind drone drowned out the sound of police cruisers pacing the frozen perimeter fences outside.
- Visual & Lyrics Prompt: Surrealist view from inside an empty mall fountain looking upward at an optical mirage of glowing arcade cabinets floating upside down in the atrium mist, bathed in deep emerald and slate-blue haze.

Track 3: Zero-Crossing Parhelion
- Story & Context: When municipal demolition bulldozers finally breached the Galleria’s plywood barricades at daybreak, they found no teenagers—only a fully automated installation constructed from thirty interconnected arcade boards and a mechanical bellows blowing into a suspended clarinet. The contraption was running an infinite 156-BPM schranz rhythm that rattled the structural beams, causing pulverized drywall dust to hang in the morning sunbeams like a blinding, artificial parhelion cloud. Scrawled across the escalator glass was a final hook: "Leave the coins in our mouths when the roof caves in." Even as the wrecking claw took down the east mezzanine, the unyielding, trance-inducing bass pulse resonated through the foundations, shaking the earth long after the power was cut.
